# Personal Knowledge Ecosystem — Structured Content

## Title
Personal Knowledge Ecosystem: System Overview

## Learning Objectives
1. Understand the scale of the knowledge base (2,500+ pages)
2. See the automated pipeline architecture at a glance
3. Identify the tooling and scheduling layer

---

## Section 1: Knowledge Wiki — The Core

**Key Concept**: A Wikipedia-style personal knowledge base organized into 6 categories

**Content**:
- 1,755 concept pages — interconnected ideas and frameworks
- 347 entity pages — people, books, places, things
- 410 source documents — raw reference material
- 26 comparison pages — side-by-side analyses
- 20 query pages — saved research questions
- 36 top-level markdown files — overview and meta pages

**Visual Element**: Large numeral "2,500+" as hero number, with category breakdown as smaller tiles

**Text Labels**: Concepts 1,755 | Entities 347 | Sources 410 | Comparisons 26 | Queries 20

---

## Section 2: Knowledge Domains

**Key Concept**: Wiki covers 6 major domains

**Content**:
- Cooking & Gastronomy (coffee, wok, regional cuisines)
- Photography (composition, lighting, post-processing)
- Personal Finance (investing, retirement, tax strategy)
- Decision Science (cognitive biases, Bayesian thinking, mental models)
- Jazz & Music Theory (bebop, Miles Davis, Thelonious Monk)
- Botany & Urban Ecology

**Visual Element**: 6 domain icons in a grid

**Text Labels**: Cooking | Photography | Finance | Decision Science | Jazz | Botany

---

## Section 3: Automated Ingestion Pipeline

**Key Concept**: 4 pipelines automatically process knowledge from raw sources to searchable format

**Content**:
1. Books Pipeline: .txt → unified_books/ → skills
2. Videos Pipeline: YouTube Watch Later → unified_videos_improved/
3. GBrain Export Pipeline: kb.md → GBrain database
4. NotebookLM Sync Pipeline: wiki updates → NotebookLM notebooks

**Visual Element**: Flow diagram with 4 stages, arrows showing direction

**Text Labels**: Source → Convert → Enrich → Index → Embed

---

## Section 4: Tooling Layer

**Key Concept**: 3 custom CLI tools provide unified interfaces

**Content**:
- knowledge-connect: Unified search across GBrain, books, NotebookLM, videos
- book-pipeline: Health monitoring for all 4 knowledge pipelines
- gbrain-notebooklm-bridge: Bidirectional sync between GBrain and NotebookLM

**Visual Element**: 3 tool cards with icons

**Text Labels**: knowledge-connect | book-pipeline | gbrain-notebooklm-bridge

---

## Section 5: Automation Schedule

**Key Concept**: 12 cron jobs run on schedules from every 15 minutes to weekly

**Content**:
- Every 15 min: GBrain Live Sync, LLM-wiki delta sync, Pipeline status check
- Every 6 hours: AI/ML Notebook update
- Daily (2AM): GBrain Dream Cycle
- Daily (3AM): GBrain PGLite export backup
- Daily (9AM): GBrain update check
- Weekly (Mon 6AM): GBrain health check + Vault defrag
- Weekly (Sun 9PM): Conversation review

**Visual Element**: Timeline or clock visualization with job frequency

**Text Labels**: 12 cron jobs | 15min → weekly | 4 pipelines | 3 CLI tools

---

## Section 6: System Health

**Key Concept**: GBrain knowledge graph health monitoring

**Content**:
- GBrain health score: 75/100 (unhealthy)
- Issue: vector extension missing ($libdir/vector)
- Schema version: 2
- Wiki index: 515 lines, last updated 2026-04-29
- Activity log: 1,251 lines of tracked changes

**Visual Element**: Health score gauge or meter

**Text Labels**: Health: 75/100 | Schema v2 | Vector extension: missing

---

## Design Instructions
- Use vibrant, clean flat vector style
- Emphasize large numbers for scale metrics
- Show flow/pipeline as connected stages
- Keep text minimal — let numbers and icons carry the message
- Color code: Wiki (blue), Pipeline (green), Tools (orange), Cron (purple)
